## SDKs — install + connect + first call

Pick the developer's language. Default data target `localhost:50051` (plaintext
in dev). **Set `authTarget` too whenever the app uses auth/native services.**
Current published baseline is **UDB 0.5.8** with wire protocol **1.0.0**; keep
the broker and SDK package on the same product version unless deliberately
testing compatibility. The platform-service wave (Vault, Metering, Scheduler,
Search, Webhook, Workflow, Lock, LiveQuery, Config, Backup, Embedding) and the
consistency/idempotency contract below are stable.

**Behavior notes for consumers (read before upgrading from 0.4.x):**
**(1) Soft-delete is the default read scope** — on a `soft_delete` table,
`Delete` tombstones the row (idempotent `UPDATE`) and ordinary `Select` results
EXCLUDE tombstoned rows automatically. **(2) Opaque row-revision (ETag) CAS** —
reads can return a `revision`; `Update`/`Delete`/`BulkCas` accept
`expected_revision` even with no `version` column. **(3) `BulkCas`** — a bounded
tenant-scoped batch of conditional single-row updates in one tx; a per-item miss
is `conflicted`, not a whole-batch failure, so a keyed partial retry is safe.
**(4) Storage hard-delete** — `DeleteFile` takes `DeleteMode` (`SOFT`/`HARD`);
`is_public`/size are immutable at finalize. **(5) Page tokens are query-bound** —
reuse under a different filter/sort/fields → `FAILED_PRECONDITION`. **(6)
Idempotency is input-bound** — replaying a key with different inputs →
`FAILED_PRECONDITION`, not a bogus success. **(7) There is no separate `Insert`
RPC** — to insert, call `Upsert` with **no `conflict_fields`** (see *CRUD →
Inserting a new row*).

