## SDK cookbook (per language, deeper)

Every SDK exposes the same three things: a **DataBroker** client (data plane), an
**Auth** client + native clients (control plane), and a **metadata/credentials**
object with hot-swap. Below: the auth→CRUD→native shape per language. Route
native clients to `authTarget`; always set `purpose` and the tenant UUID.

### Go
```go
// Enterprise (human): one-call login + adopt UUID + background refresh.
sess, _ := udbclient.ConnectEnterprise(ctx, udbclient.EnterpriseConfig{
    Target: "localhost:50051", AuthTarget: "localhost:50061",
    Username: "admin", Password: pass, TenantCode: "acme", ProjectID: "default",
    Scopes: []string{"udb:read", "udb:write"}})
defer sess.Close()
t := sess.CanonicalTenantID                              // the UUID, use in filters
sess.Data.Broker.Upsert(sess.DataContext(ctx), &entityv1.UpsertRequest{
    MessageType: "shop.v1.Customer", ConflictFields: []string{"customer_id"},
    Payload: pb(map[string]any{"customer_id": "c1", "tenant_id": t, "email": "a@x.com"}),
    IdempotencyKey: "c1-create"})
// Native: NativeContext + NativeConn.
tenant := tenantv1.NewTenantServiceClient(sess.NativeConn())
tenant.EnsureTenant(sess.NativeContext(ctx), &tenantv1.EnsureTenantRequest{Code: "acme"})

// Service (machine): static API key, no refresh token exists for service accounts.
u, _ := udbclient.NewUdb(ctx, udbclient.Config{Target: "localhost:50051",
    AuthTarget: "localhost:50061", TenantID: tenantUUID, ProjectID: "default",
    Scopes: []string{"udb:read","udb:write"},
    Credentials: udbclient.Credentials{APIKey: "udbk_…"}})
// on expiry: exchange the key → bearer, then u.SetAuthorization(tok) (hot-swap)
```

### TypeScript
```ts
const udb = await UdbProject.connectEnterprise({
  target: "localhost:50051", authTarget: "localhost:50061",
  username: "admin", password, tenantCode: "acme", projectId: "default",
  scopes: ["udb:read", "udb:write"],
});
const t = udb.canonicalTenantId;
await udb.entity("shop.v1.Customer").upsert(
  { customer_id: "c1", tenant_id: t, email: "a@x.com" },
  { conflictFields: ["customer_id"], idempotencyKey: "c1-create" });
const rs = await udb.entity("shop.v1.Customer").select({ limit: 50 });
// native: udb.native.TenantService.ensureTenant({ code: "acme" });
// service: new UdbProject({ credentials: { apiKey: "udbk_…" } })  // or bearerToken
```

### Python
```python
udb = create_udb(target="localhost:50051", auth_target="localhost:50061")
udb.login_and_adopt_tenant("admin", password)           # adopts canonical UUID
t = udb.config.tenant_id
udb.data.upsert(message_type="shop.v1.Customer",
                record={"customer_id": "c1", "tenant_id": t, "email": "a@x.com"},
                conflict_fields=("customer_id",), idempotency_key="c1-create")
rows = udb.data.select(message_type="shop.v1.Customer", limit=50)
# native: udb.native.TenantService.EnsureTenant(...)
# service: create_udb(..., api_key="udbk_…")   # static credential, you own lifetime
```

### Java / C# / PHP
Same three parts. Java/C#: `UdbProject` with data+auth targets and a
`Credentials` object (bearer or api-key), `select/upsert` on the data client,
generated native clients on the auth channel; `MutationOutcome` exposes
`wasDuplicate`. PHP/Laravel: `UdbClient(['endpoint'=>…])` + `UdbMetadata`; native
services via the generated clients pointed at the auth endpoint; `wasReplay($r)`
for idempotent-replay detection.

**Credential hot-swap (all SDKs):** `set_credentials()` / `SetAuthorization` /
`SetAPIKey` swaps the token without rebuilding the channel — use it on rotation
and on API-key→bearer re-exchange.

