## Production hardening (broker-side quickref)

For a hardened deployment (see `docs/enterprise-deployment.md` for the full
checklist):
- `UDB_ENV=production` (fails closed on dev shortcuts), `UDB_TLS_REQUIRED=true`,
  `UDB_MTLS_REQUIRED=true` (or `UDB_TRUSTED_TRANSPORT=true` behind a terminating
  proxy/mesh).
- Real RS256 keys (`UDB_JWT_PRIVATE_KEY`/`UDB_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY` or
  `UDB_JWT_JWKS_URL`), a strong `UDB_ENCRYPTION_KEY`, and matching
  `UDB_PASSWORD_HASH_SECRET`/`UDB_SESSION_HASH_SECRET`.
- **No** `UDB_ABAC_DEFAULT_ALLOW`, **no** `UDB_ALLOW_HEADER_SCOPES` (the latter is
  a hard production error).
- Seed real least-privilege `policy_rules` (roles + bindings), not a wildcard.
- Expose `UDB_AUTH_GRPC_ADDR` only on a trusted interface; keep the WebRTC peer
  plane scoped.
- Pooler-safe DSN; watch CRLF in `.env`. If a pooler advisory lock wedges startup,
  `udb admin release-lock`. Opaque `INTERNAL` on a write → `UDB_VERBOSE_DB_ERRORS`
  to see the cause. Run `udb doctor --enterprise` + `udb requirements` before
  every deploy. `udb deploy plan|apply|render` turns a `udb.deploy.yaml` into all
  of the above idempotently.

