## CLI — the `udb` binary (reference)

**Discover it:** `udb --help` / `udb help` (grouped list), `udb <cmd> --help` or
`udb help <cmd>` (usage + flags + example), `udb --version`. Unknown commands get
a "did you mean …?" suggestion.

**Bring-up & inspection**
| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `udb proto export --out proto` | Vendor UDB's annotation protos so app protos can `import "udb/core/common/v1/db.proto"`. |
| `udb serve proto "" 0.0.0.0:50051` | Start the broker (syncs schema from protos on boot; control-plane listener at port+10). Wait for the `… is ready: data=… auth=…` line. |
| `udb doctor [--with-probes] [--enterprise] [--consumer --key --entity]` | Env + backend readiness. `--enterprise` = one-shot preflight (encryption/password/session/auth-plane/redis/ABAC) AND manifest-aware (reports required backends your protos declare but you haven't configured). `--consumer --key <k> --entity <e>` dials a running broker and probes the authn→authz chain, surfacing the exact PERMISSION_DENIED reason. |
| `udb requirements [--json]` | The resolved backend contract for the manifest (each required backend, env vars, configured?, fatal/degraded, suggested fix). Non-zero exit if a fatal backend is unset — run BEFORE first startup. |
| `udb plan` / `udb drift` / `udb lint` | Migration diff + gates / manifest-vs-live drift / annotation lint. |
| `udb native list / manifest / docs / contract-diff` | Inspect the native service contract; diff between versions. |
| `udb sdk generate --lang <l>` / `sdk list-langs` / `sdk manifest` | Generate/refresh SDK clients; dump the authoritative RPC manifest. |
| `udb orm scaffold` | Generate typed repository/entity models from the manifest. |
| `udb compat-matrix` | The authoritative annotation surface (from the parser). |
| `udb dev up / down / smoke` | Local sandbox via the bundled compose (from a repo checkout). |
| `udb init` / `udb init-project` (= `udb scaffold`) | Scaffold a project (proto/config/compose/6 client examples). Mind `UDB_PROTO_NAMESPACE`. |

**Auth & policy**
| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `udb auth bootstrap user --username … --tenant acme …` | First offline admin. Prints the canonical tenant UUID — **capture it**. Seeds only the org-owner wildcard policy; you still seed per-entity rows. |
| `udb auth api-key-create …` | Mint an API key (owner must be an active service account + grant). |
| `udb auth policy put --subject role:R --action '*' --resource <fqn> --effect allow --tenant <UUID>` | Write a `policy_rules` Allow via `PutAuthzPolicy` (needs a running broker). |
| `udb auth role bind --principal <id> --role R --tenant <UUID>` | Bind a principal to a role. |
| `udb auth relation put …` | Write a ReBAC tuple. |
| `udb auth grant …` | Service-account grant lifecycle. |
| `udb authz seed --tenant <UUID> [--role R] [--entity <fqn>…] [--emit <file>]` | THE straightforward offline seeder: role-gated Allow rows (`Select`/`Upsert`/`Delete`/`Update`/`BulkCas` — validated tokens) directly into `udb_authz.policy_rules` (Postgres-direct, idempotent + atomic). Then bind principals with `udb auth role bind`. |
| `udb policy-seed` (with `UDB_ABAC_POLICY_FILE`) | Print the atomic `policy_rules` INSERT SQL to stdout → pipe to `psql`. Offline. |
| `udb policy-lint` | Lint an offline policy file (CI-safe, non-zero on breakage). |
| `udb authz simulate` | "What would change if this policy bundle shipped" (read-only). |

**Enterprise**
| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `udb deploy plan\|apply\|render` | Declarative `udb.deploy.yaml` → full production env (mTLS/JWT/RLS/audit) + idempotent bootstrap of tenants/service-accounts/grants/api-keys/policies. |
| `udb admin force-sync \| release-lock \| verify-audit \| reset-db` | Operate a running deployment (release a stuck pooler advisory lock, force a migration, etc.). |
| `udb compliance evidence \| export` | Compliance evidence bundle. |

