## Scopes & purpose conventions

**Scopes** gate operations. Data-plane conventions: `udb:read`, `udb:write` (and
your policy's `required_scopes` refine an Allow). Native-plane: one scope per RPC,
`udb:<service>:<kebab-method>` (e.g. `udb:vault:put-secret`,
`udb:authn:create-user`, `udb:storage:register-upload`). Broad admin scopes that
cover any non-public native RPC: `*`, `udb:*`, `udb:admin`, `udb:auth:admin`.
Grant a service **only** the scopes it needs (its `ServiceAccountGrant` rejects
admin/owner/wildcard). Look up exact scopes in
`docs/generated/authn-authz-rpc-inventory.md`.

**Purpose** (`x-purpose`) is the request's declared intent (`web.request`,
`billing.api`, `analytics.export`, …). It is **required** on tenant-scoped data
ops (empty → denied before authz). It can be matched by a policy's `purpose`
attribute (leave empty/`*` in policies unless you're purpose-gating). Use a
stable, meaningful value per call-site — it appears in audit records.

