## Integration recipes (by app shape)

- **Multi-tenant web API backend.** One deployment, many tenants. On each request
  resolve the caller's tenant (from their session/JWT), set `tenant_id`=UUID +
  `purpose`="web.request" + `user_id`, and CRUD by `message_type`. Authorize with
  a per-tenant role bound to the user. Use `read_your_writes` fences after writes
  that the same request re-reads. Rotate the user bearer with `set_credentials()`.
- **Background worker / cron consumer.** A service account with an API key and a
  narrow grant (`udb:read` + the specific writes it does). Static credential;
  re-exchange the key → bearer on expiry. Idempotent writes with a stable
  `idempotency_key` (e.g. the source event id) so retries are safe. Subscribe to
  `PublishCDC` (resumable) rather than polling.
- **Data pipeline / ETL.** Service account; batch streams (`BatchSelect`/
  `BatchUpsert`) for volume; `bounded_staleness`/`replica_bounded` reads to spare
  the leader; `BulkCas` for conditional batch updates. Meter throughput via
  MeteringService.
- **Analytics / reporting.** Read replica or ClickHouse backend via
  `AnalyticalQuery`; `projection_ok`/`cache_ok` consistency; SearchService for
  full-text/vector.
- **Realtime app.** LiveQueryService `Subscribe` for change streams; WebRTC for
  media (peer plane `:50071`); NotificationService for push.

## Multi-tenancy patterns

- **Tenant = the canonical UUID.** Provision with `TenantService.EnsureTenant`;
  adopt `principal.tenant_id`. Every tenant-scoped table has a tenant column;
  every read/write is auto-filtered and cross-tenant reads are impossible (a
  foreign row is indistinguishable from a missing one — `NOT_FOUND`).
- **Project** (`project_id`) sub-scopes a tenant's catalog; on native storage/
  asset RPCs it is UUID-only.
- **Policy per tenant:** seed `policy_rules` with `tenant_id`=each tenant's UUID
  (or empty/`*` for a platform-wide rule). A platform admin role with empty
  `tenant_id` spans tenants — use sparingly.
- **Isolation proof:** the enterprise examples include a cross-tenant read that
  MUST return empty — keep it as a test.

## Streaming & batch

- **`SelectV2`** streams `RecordBatchV2` frames for large result sets — consume
  incrementally instead of one huge `RecordSet`.
- **`BatchSelect` / `BatchUpsert`** are bidirectional streams: one wildcard authz
  gate up front, then per-item authorization as items flow. Use for bulk load /
  fan-out.
- **`BulkCas`** is a single unary bounded batch (not a stream) of conditional
  single-row updates in one tx.
- All streams honor tenant isolation and idempotency per item.

## Observability

- Always set `x-correlation-id`/`x-request-id` (SDKs auto-attach) — they thread
  through logs, audit, and native RPCs (many require request context).
- Every authorized mutation and native admin action is audited (tenant, subject,
  purpose, decision id). Denials carry a `policy_decision_id` you can correlate.
- The typed `ErrorDetail` trailer gives machine-readable failure info
  (kind/retryable/retry_after_ms/field_violations) — log that, not the string.
- `GetHealthReport`/`GetCapabilities` expose readiness + the live RPC surface;
  `udb doctor` (and `--consumer`) probe from outside.

## Glossary

- **message_type** — a proto message's fully-qualified name; the entity handle
  for every data RPC.
- **manifest / catalog** — the normalized, checksummed schema UDB derives from
  your protos; the catalog version travels in metadata.
- **tenant** — the isolation boundary, a canonical UUID (human code is an alias).
- **project** — a sub-scope of a tenant's catalog.
- **purpose** — declared request intent; required on tenant-scoped data ops.
- **scope** — a capability token string (`udb:read`, `udb:vault:put-secret`).
- **grant (ServiceAccountGrant)** — the operator-approved scope envelope a
  service account must have to authenticate.
- **policy (policy_rules)** — a Casbin rule authorizing data-plane CRUD.
- **role / role binding** — a named bundle of policies; bind principals to it.
- **relationship tuple** — a ReBAC edge for relationship-based authorization.
- **write receipt / read fence** — the token a mutation returns / the read
  precondition built from it for read-your-writes.
- **idempotency_key** — a stable key that makes a mutation replay-safe.
- **revision (ETag)** — an opaque per-row version for optimistic-concurrency CAS.
- **native plane / data plane** — the control-plane services (`:50061`) vs the
  DataBroker CRUD (`:50051`).

